{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790314446,"nonce":"ZxhWZ8NFvn6vHZSP/cTN/YEqszs=","title":"hexiom2 speed kernel prints no solution since per-signature instances (80749056)","message":"`speed/run.py --only hexiom2` fails with the kernel's own check, `AssertionError: got a wrong answer:` followed by an empty capture: `solve_file` for level 36 prints nothing into the StringIO that stands in for sys.stdout (a plain print through a redirected sys.stdout is captured correctly, so the solver itself finds no solution or skips its output).\n\nReproducer: stage crates/zyntax_python/benchmarks/speed/kernels/hexiom2.py with shims/util.py and shims/optparse.py in one directory, then `ZYPY_LLVM=1 zypy run hexiom2.py -n 1`. CPython and PyPy print the expected board.\n\nDeterministic, both machines (Mac arm64, NUC x86_64), with the LLVM tier on or off and with ZYNTAX_DISABLE_OSR=1.\n\nBisected on the NUC with release llvm-backend builds: efedddf8 prints the right board (11.1 s), 80749056 \"Python: per-signature instances of closed items\" prints nothing, as do e240a9a2, 678f49eb (wave-1 base) and 5a6d14fd (perf-integration head). Older binaries (Sep 21 main, the Sep 24 18:06 base-w2 build) pass.","files":null}]}